                <pb facs="0899" n="815" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg815"/>

                <head>No. 407.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Curry to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-10-22"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 22, 1886</date>.
                        (Received October 22—10 a.m.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Curry informs Mr. Bayard that, according to a telegram which he has received
                    on that day, he makes the renewal of the agreement depend upon the inclusion
                    therein of cargoes carried in ships of the United States from any foreign
                    country. He desires to be informed whether this condition is indispensable to
                    the conclusion of an agreement.</p>
            </div>
